# FEASIBILITY PROBE grammar — not the extraction grammar.
#
# The real GBNF grammar is Devansh's and lives in /src/extraction (CLAUDE.md
# §15). This one exists to test a single claim from the project docs:
#
#   "A hand-written grammar constrains a date field to \d{2}/\d{2}/\d{4}
#    *at the token level* — a malformed date becomes structurally unreachable
#    rather than caught afterwards."
#
# Note what this grammar does NOT allow: a null. That is deliberate — it is the
# variant that tests what happens when the model has no date to give.

root        ::= "{" ws "\"deadline\":" ws date ws "}"
date        ::= "\"" digit digit "/" digit digit "/" digit digit digit digit "\""
digit       ::= [0-9]
ws          ::= [ \t\n]*
